ok program by name on the PATH: true started (ok) and answers 0
ok program false: error() says the code it ended with
ok program from a list: code() waits and answers its exit code
ok program started again after it ended, and return() answers its code
ok program an argument with a space in it stays one argument
ok program not on the PATH: ok() is false and error() says so
ok program not on the PATH answers 127, as a shell does
ok program ended by a signal answers 128 + the signal
ok program start("hide") throws its output away and still answers
ok program from a list held in a name: its code, then == for two names and for two programs
ok bash line's pipe and > wrote its file
ok bash line reads || and $(( ))
ok bash line's code is the line's
ok bash line with a missing command started (ok) and answers bash's 127
ok bash start() answers while the line still waits for its input
ok bash pass() types lines in, read in order
ok bash a capsule taking a program takes a bash line
ok bash a bash parameter makes a line from a string
ok bash a program name holds a bash line, the same one
ok program end() stops it and answers 143
ok program stopped: error() names the signal
ok program exit(), quit() and shutdown() are end()
ok program displays as (program sh -c exit 3, ended with 3)
ok bash line displays as (bash exit 0, ended with 0)
